\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}

\title{Seat Licence Renewal Memo}
\author{Platform Team}
\date{}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Current Spend}
The licence costs \$100 per seat. We hold 42 seats, and the
vendor bills annually in advance. The one-off setup fee of
\$250 was paid last year and does not recur.

\section{Forecast}
If headcount grows as planned, the renewal quote scales
linearly: the finance model uses $C = 100n$ for $n$ seats
and ignores the setup fee entirely. Any discount negotiation
must close before the end of the quarter, because the
auto-renewal clause triggers thirty days ahead of the
anniversary date.

\section{Action}
Renew as is, but ask procurement to test a two-year
commitment in exchange for a modest per-seat reduction.
\end{document}

